mastery.question_text:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.42]
\draw (0,0) -- (10,0) node[midway,below,font=\small] {$10\text{ m}$};
\draw (10,0) -- (10,7) node[midway,right,font=\small] {$7\text{ m}$};
\draw (10,7) -- (6,7);
\draw (6,7) -- (6,3) node[midway,left,font=\small] {$4\text{ m}$};
\draw (6,3) -- (2,3);
\draw (2,3) -- (2,11) node[midway,right,font=\small] {$x$};
\draw (2,11) -- (0,11) node[midway,above,font=\small] {$2\text{ m}$};
\draw (0,11) -- (0,0) node[midway,left,font=\small] {$11\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
All angles are right angles. Find the length marked $x$.

mastery.solution_text:
The sides pointing up must add to the same total as the sides pointing down. The $4\text{ m}$ step points down, so it joins the $11\text{ m}$ left side.
$7+x=4+11$
$x=15-7$
$=8\text{ m}$

